<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsuruoka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsuruoka is a city on the Shōnai plain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamagata-prefecture">Yamagata Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. From 1622 it was the castle town of the Sakai clan, lords of the Shōnai Domain, whose domain school, the Chidōkan, still stands. Close to the sacred mountains of Dewa Sanzan, it remains the cultural centre of the Shōnai region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tsuruoka.jpg" alt="Tsuruoka" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 水だらけのプール · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tsuruoka_montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
